      "writtenOn": "2026-05-22T19:05:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "SkGlyphRect is basically like Graphite\u0027s Rect that is optimized for SIMD accumulation and intersection tests.  Instead of jumping back to SkPoint and SkRect for this loop, we should just use `SkGlyphRect(skglyph::rect_union(SkGlyphRect, SkGlyphRect);`. SkGyphRect also has an offset function so we can account for the top left point of the run.\n\nIf we initialize `boundingRect` to be the inverted infinite, then the first loop through\u0027s union will be no different and we avoid a branch.  We can just convert to SkRect at the end.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 132,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "fe27b485d37b67755bb71083cc738ac6f39d6300",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
